# Phase 1: Create evolution-auto-runner.cjs

## Overview

New SessionStart hook in `D:\code\invesments\master_investments\.claude\hooks\` that checks 4 staleness conditions and spawns Python evolution scripts as detached background processes.

## Related Code Files

- Create: `D:\code\invesments\master_investments\.claude\hooks\evolution-auto-runner.cjs`
- Read (existing patterns): `D:\code\invesments\master_investments\.claude\hooks\cron-weekly-runner.cjs`

## Architecture

```
SessionStart → evolution-auto-runner.cjs
  ├── Check 1: evolution_log.json last cycle >7 days?
  │   YES → spawn auto_evolve.py (detached)
  ├── Check 2: evolution-config.json last_run >7 days?
  │   YES → spawn scheduled-evolution-loop.py (detached)
  ├── Check 3: pending-index.json has expired + last batch-verify >3 days?
  │   YES → spawn batch-auto-verify.py --all-expired (detached)
  └── Check 4: knowledge staleness >50% + last hunt >14 days?
      YES → spawn knowledge_hunter.py (detached)
```

## Implementation Steps

1. Create hook file following `cron-weekly-runner.cjs` pattern (fail-open, `isHookEnabled` check)
2. Implement 4 checker functions, each with:
   - Read timestamp from respective JSON/log file
   - Compare against threshold
   - If due: create lock file, spawn detached process, unref
3. Each checker has independent lock file in `.logs/` (10-min expiry)
4. Log all actions to `.logs/evolution-auto-runner.log`

### Checker Details

| # | Data File | Threshold | Script to Spawn | Args |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | `data/deep-intelligence/evolution_log.json` → last cycle timestamp | 7 days | `auto_evolve.py` | (none) |
| 2 | `.claude/data/evolution-config.json` → `last_run` | 7 days | `scheduled-evolution-loop.py` | (none) |
| 3 | `.logs/batch-verify-last-run.txt` (create if missing) | 3 days | `batch-auto-verify.py` | `--all-expired` |
| 4 | `data/deep-intelligence/evolution_log.json` → last hunt timestamp | 14 days | `knowledge_hunter.py` | (none, runs `hunt_all()` internally) |

